{
  "rationale": "Evidence: all 60 development trials across oval, s-bend and slalom ended off_track with zero completions. Progress was only 0.04 to 0.23, and max_error sits at the off-track limit of 0.06 m. Line-loss events were 1 to 2 per run, so the robot loses the tape entirely before it leaves the track. RMS error (about 0.027) and steering oscillation (0.06 to 0.2) are modest. Iteration 1 (kp 2.5, kd 0.15, base 1.2) roughly doubled the score over iteration 0, which confirms that damping and a slower speed help. The remaining failure is loss of the line on the first real excursion.\n\nHypothesis: the sensor array is too narrow. The five sensors span only x = ±0.03 m. With a 12 mm footprint and a 12.5 mm tape half-width, the outer sensors see tape only once the robot is about 1.2 cm off-centre, and all sensors go blank at roughly 2 to 3 cm of error. Once the line is lost, the controller falls back to a fixed-direction search at throttle 0.35 and the robot leaves the 6 cm limit. A wider array of seven sensors spanning x = ±0.06 m keeps the tape visible at larger errors, so the controller can still steer back.\n\nChanges: (1) Replace the five-sensor array with seven sensors at x = -0.06, -0.04, -0.02, 0, 0.02, 0.04, 0.06 m, all at y = 0.04 m. (2) Use weights -2, -1.3, -0.6, 0, 0.6, 1.3, 2 so the signal scale stays near the earlier ±2 range. (3) Keep base_speed 1.2, kp 2.5, ki 0, kd 0.15 and line_loss last_direction, so this race isolates the sensor change. Geometry other than the sensors is unchanged. Body width is also unchanged, because the off-track limit stays at 0.06 m for any width up to 0.18 m.\n\nExpected result: fewer line-loss events, more progress per run (target above 0.4 on at least one track), and a higher score. A completion inside 3 s is still unlikely at 1.2 m/s.\n\nHypotheses to check next: if the robot still leaves with few line-loss events, the cause is steering lag on bends, and I will raise kp or kd. If steering_oscillation rises sharply, the wider array has increased gain and I will lower kp. If the line is still lost, I will test a lower base_speed or a larger sensor_size of 0.016.",
